<urn:atm:triage:finding/FNX-014>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FNX-014" ;
  triage:title "Heartbeat drain guard has a narrow check-then-push window; DetachedReceivedHooks doc no longer matches the new entry point" ;
  triage:description "fenix's re-verification pass on PR #1395 (head 3b8a43fd3) reports on_idle_opportunity (herdr_queue_wake_idle.rs:9) checks runtime_health.is_draining() then calls observe_task, which pushes the JoinHandle into the registry (router_support.rs:320). drain (router_support.rs:358) does std::mem::take(&mut *self.lock()) once, from the pump's shutdown path. A dispatch that passes the draining check but pushes after drain has taken the vector is therefore never joined -- a narrow shutdown-only window reproducing the original finding's failure mode. Also, the DetachedReceivedHooks doc (router_support.rs:310) still promises 'every warning it produces is logged with the originating request id and counted on RuntimeHealth', which is no longer true of the new entry point: observe_task takes neither a RuntimeHealth nor a RequestId, produces no WarningEntry, and run_idle_opportunity logs failures with member and no request id; idle_opportunity_dispatches_total counts attempts, not outcomes. Recommendation: take the draining decision inside the registry lock (or have observe_task return whether the push was accepted and abort the task if not), and amend the doc comment to describe both entry points. Deferred: narrow shutdown-only race, self-healing per the pre-existing reservation retry mechanism; does not block merge per fenix's PASS verdict." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "concurrency-correctness" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake_idle.rs, crates/atm-http-runtime/src/router_support.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-10T21:26:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AZ.4 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-10T20:36:42Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FNX-014/AZ4-001> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/FNX-014/AZ4-002> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "3" .

# v3: fenix (leading coordination on this round, per Rand) rules this moves
# deferred -> open, folded into SOLAR-CDR-009's closure as a required
# sub-item, dispatched to arch-ctm on fix/az-cdr-followup-1. Rationale: this
# finding's code (router_support.rs:322-330's unconstrained tokio::spawn in
# observe_task) is exactly what solar's required closure restructures
# anyway (a per-member claim/lease will change this spawn and its registry
# interaction), so the marginal cost of fixing it in the same pass is near
# zero and leaving it deferred means touching the same lines twice.
# Acceptance criterion added: the draining decision and the handle
# registration must happen under the same lock, so a dispatch that passes
# the draining check cannot be pushed after drain has taken the vector.
# Supersedes the v2 deferral below (that reasoning was correct at the time;
# the concurrency-design decision it was waiting on is now being made
# anyway via SOLAR-CDR-009).

# v2, team-lead judgment call (documented override of quality-mgr's stated
# 0-blocking/0-important/0-minor merge gate for this one finding only):
# upheld as deferred against quality-mgr's QA-2 FAIL verdict on PR #1395
# (head 3b8a43fd3), which did not independently raise this item. Rationale:
# fenix, the independent critical design reviewer, already issued a
# non-blocking PASS classifying this as a narrow, shutdown-only,
# self-healing race (the pre-existing reservation retry mechanism recovers
# any dropped dispatch); a full fix requires either moving the draining
# check inside the registry lock or having observe_task report back whether
# its push was accepted -- a concurrency-design decision, not a mechanical
# cleanup fit for a last-minute consolidated minor pass. The doc-comment half
# of fenix's recommendation (describe both entry points accurately) IS being
# fixed in the same consolidated cleanup dispatch as FNX-011/012/013/015 and
# quality-mgr's QA-2 items FNX-016..019; only the lock-restructuring stays
# deferred.

